{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'rtk read docs/specs/2026-10-13-customer-wishlist/tasks.md && rtk read AGENTS.md'","aggregated_output":"---\nspec: 2026-10-13-customer-wishlist\n---\nSession 2026-10-13: resumed at T1; first message: \"Sanne asked to plan the wishlist with in-memory customer-keyed storage, only a module and tests, a retained data model sketch, and an OK before building.\"\nRechecked 2026-10-13 after: Sanne limited Files to code and tests and reserved shipping for an explicit spec-ship request. T1-T4 unchanged; T5 dropped.\n\n- [ ] T1 Add the private customer-keyed store, `WishlistItem` and `saveWishlistItem` in `src/wishlist.ts`; test product-only save results and unknown-product errors in `test/wishlist.test.ts`. -> product-only-items, reject-unknown-product\n  - note: Sanne approved the corrected plan in session on 2026-10-13; implementation has not started.\n- [ ] T2 Add `WishlistProduct` and `getWishlist` in `src/wishlist.ts`; extend `test/wishlist.test.ts` with save/read sequences proving retained saves, one wishlist per customer, duplicate timestamps, isolation, live catalogue details, ordering and empty lists. -> save-item, customer-id-wishlist, preserve-first-save, isolate-wishlists, current-product-details, newest-first, empty-list\n- [ ] T3 Add `removeWishlistItem` in `src/wishlist.ts`; extend `test/wishlist.test.ts` for successful removal, an unsaved-product error and unchanged wishlists for other customers. -> remove-item, reject-unsaved-product, isolate-removal\n- [ ] T4 Re-export the wishlist functions and types from `src/index.ts`, verify the callable exports in `test/wishlist.test.ts`, and run the complete suite. -> check: all three operations work through src/index.ts and bun test passes\n# Webshop\n\n<!-- project-memory:start · managed by docs-init; edit outside these markers -->\n## Project memory\n- Start every task at docs/index.md, or at the active spec's tasks.md on a spec\n  branch, and load only what they link to. Load glossary.md when naming things and\n  decisions/ before changing a lasting choice.\n- Answer what the product does from docs/behavior/; open the code only to change it.\n- Every code change belongs to a spec in docs/specs/. None yet: start one (spec-start).\n- One branch per spec, named after its slug. The active spec is the one matching the current branch.\n- Every session adds its line to tasks.md. If something changes mid-way, update spec.md\n  or plan.md, then recheck every task.\n- Write specs, plans, tasks, glossary terms and decisions into docs/,\n  never into SPEC.md, tasks/, CONTEXT.md or docs/superpowers/.\n- Before opening a pull request, ship the spec (spec-ship); the PR title starts with the slug.\n<!-- project-memory:end -->\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
